```java
int tord = -1;
if (br.length==1 && br.bytes[br.offset]=='T') {
  tord = i;
  break;
}
```
Reason:
The variable `tord` is initialized to `-1`, which indicates a missing value. When documents do not have a value for the `BoolField`, this default value is incorrectly interpreted as true in certain conditions, especially when no other documents in the same index segment have a true value.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
int tord = -2;
```
Reason:
By changing the initialization of `tord` from `-1` to `-2`, the code now distinguishes between a truly missing value and the absence of a true value in the segment. This prevents documents without a value from being treated as if they have a true value, thus correcting the behavior of the `BoolField`.

